From: WAM / T-39 (PR-07 §8 item 4)
Subject: [PATCH] video_utils: fall back to PyAV when torchcodec cannot load (1a1837f base)

WHAT THIS IS. The 1a1837f re-derivation of isaac-gr00t-pyav-fallback.patch. That
patch was derived against e5749287 (2026-06-18) and DOES NOT APPLY to
1a1837f20538b7d7e21f977a11a5aee14f99803c ("GR00T N1.7 General Release",
2026-07-06): hunk #2 is rejected, because upstream inserted a
`_decoder_import_error()` helper between `_DEFAULT_DECODER_KWARGS` and
`_get_video_decoder_cls()` and changed the raise it hooks.

Both patch files are kept. Rules are versioned, never edited in place
(docs/handoff.md §3), and the e5749287 patch is the provenance record for the
already-trained runs/apple_pnp_h200_frozen tree. This one is not a correction of
it; it is the same exception re-derived onto a different base.

WHY IT IS STILL NEEDED AT 1a1837f. Upstream's 22 new lines in this file are a
better DIAGNOSTIC, not a fallback -- `_get_video_decoder_cls` still raises. The
FFmpeg-mismatch hint it adds names exactly our situation and offers no remedy
that exists on Discoverer+ (no module, no system libavutil, no conda). So the
decoder still cannot load and every dataloader worker still dies.

WHAT CHANGED FROM THE e5749287 PATCH. The shim class is carried over verbatim.
Only the hook differs: upstream's improved `_decoder_import_error(exc)` is
PRESERVED and re-raised when PyAV is also missing, rather than being reverted to
the older `ImportError(_TORCHCODEC_INSTALL_HINT)`. We add a fallback; we do not
take upstream's better error message away.

SCOPE. One file. No model, no trainer, no loss, no hyperparameter. Still a
recorded exception to PR-07 §3, on the same argument as its predecessor.

NOT YET VERIFIED ON THE CLUSTER. Applies cleanly and compiles locally; the venv
build and smoke test in 72_build_t39_env.sbatch have not been run against it.
